Description:
    Creates the migration for the two tables ActiveJob::Durable writes to
    (active_job_durable_runs and active_job_durable_steps).

    Without options the migration goes to db/migrate: the tables live next to
    the application's tables, and a run is created in the same transaction as
    the record that starts it.

    With --database=NAME the migration goes to that database's migrations_paths
    (from config/database.yml) and an initializer points ActiveJob::Durable at
    it. Declare the database first, or follow the printed instructions.

Example:
    bin/rails generate ajdc:install
        db/migrate/TIMESTAMP_create_active_job_durable_tables.rb

    bin/rails generate ajdc:install --database=durable
        db/durable_migrate/TIMESTAMP_create_active_job_durable_tables.rb
        config/initializers/active_job_durable.rb
